# tree288_400Gbps.topo — R3 realism stage: the tree288 scale-out tier at
# 400 Gbps host links (H100-cluster class) instead of the 100 Gbps example
# shape. Structure, latencies, and oversubscription identical to
# tree288_100Gbps.topo so the R2->R3 delta isolates scale-out bandwidth:
# 288 hosts as 12 ToRs x 24 hosts, 2:1 oversubscribed, 12 aggs (parser
# invariant: T1 Radix_Down = #ToRs = 12).
#
# NIC note: at 400 Gbps the engine's Mbps arithmetic and the pipes' ps/B
# quantisation agree exactly (4,150 B x 8 / 4e11 = 83.0 ns/frame = 4,150 x
# 20 ps), so passing -linkspeed 400000 pins the scale-out NIC to the pipes
# with zero residual. It MUST be passed: the COPY_ENG default (200,000 Mbps)
# would silently cap a 400 Gbps fabric at half rate.
Nodes 288
Tiers 2
Podsize 288

Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 400
Radix_Down 24
Radix_Up 12
Downlink_Latency_ns 1
Switch_Latency_ns 0
Oversubscribed 2

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 400
Radix_Down 12
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0
